---
title: "Vivacon - Runtime - Send a chat message in an existing conversation (AS-IS)"
---
%% Traced from code; each message names the method that performs it.
%% Evidence: docs/architecture/architecture-inventory.md section 5.
%% nginx sits on the path in the Docker/VM deployment only; with the CRA dev server
%% the browser talks to the API directly.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor A as Sender (browser)<br/>ChatPage + useSocket
    participant N as nginx<br/>/ws/ proxy
    participant I as STOMP inbound<br/>CustomInterceptor
    participant C as ChatController
    participant S as MessageServiceImpl
    participant R as JPA repositories
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant B as Simple broker<br/>(in-memory)
    actor P as Other participants<br/>(browsers)

    Note over A,B: Session setup, once per page load: App.js -> useSocket.connect()
    A->>N: SockJS handshake GET /ws/info, then upgrade
    N->>I: proxy with Upgrade / Connection headers
    Note right of I: registerStompEndpoints: Origin must match<br/>vivacon.frontend.allowed-origins, else 403
    A->>I: STOMP CONNECT, header WS-Authorization: JWT
    I->>I: preSend: JwtUtils.getUsername + loadUserByUsername,<br/>accessor.setUser(principal)
    A->>B: SUBSCRIBE /conversation/{id}/message<br/>(ids from REST GET /api/v1/conversation/id)

    Note over A,P: User presses Enter: ChatPage.sendMessage -> chatInExistedConversation
    A->>I: SEND /app/chat {conversationId, content}, WS-Authorization
    I->>C: processChatMessage(@Valid UsualTextMessage)
    C->>S: save(messageRequest)
    Note right of S: @Transactional begins
    S->>R: getCurrentAccount: AccountRepository.findByUsernameIgnoreCase
    R->>DB: SELECT account
    S->>R: ParticipantRepository.findByConversationIdAndAccountId
    R->>DB: SELECT participant

    alt sender is a participant
        S->>R: MessageRepository.save(message)
        R->>DB: INSERT message
        S->>R: ConversationRepository.updateLastModifiedAtById
        R->>DB: UPDATE conversation
        S-->>C: MessageResponse (transaction commits)
        C->>B: SimpMessagingTemplate.convertAndSend<br/>/conversation/{id}/message
        B-->>A: MESSAGE frame
        B-->>P: MESSAGE frame
        Note over A,P: useSocket.onMessageReceived -> reducer GET_RECEIVE_MESSAGE
    else not a participant
        S--xC: UnauthorizedWebSocketException (rollback)
        Note over C,A: No @MessageExceptionHandler exists, so the sender<br/>gets no reply frame (inferred from Spring default)
    end
